{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794839763,"nonce":"VJIokv+ladzZsT0uSAsV3p55DQY=","title":"An SVG captured by a translucent group stays put while rows scroll its page","message":"cn_demo, Pagination section: the chevron of a disabled button (`.cn-pagination-btn:disabled` has `opacity: 0.5`) drew where the last full paint left it while the page scrolled on rows, offset by the distance scrolled since that paint, and snapped back at rest. Enabled chevrons were fine.\n\nCause: a group with opacity captures its SVG children as ordered images (`prepare_captured_svg`). That path set no motion node ordinal, so `give_dynamic_image_slots` found no slot for the image and skipped it, leaving it unmoved. Captured images already passed `ordinal_of(tree, node)`.\n\nFix: `prepare_captured_svg` takes the ordinal, and draws with the scroll clip and the clip inside it apart (new `SvgElement::split_clip`), as captured images do, so rows can move the inner clip instead of declining. Reproduced headlessly with `cn_demo_costs` `COSTS_AT=15150 COSTS_SNAP_SCROLL=\u003cpng\u003e` (mid-scroll frame against a full paint). Guarded by the animation_paths scene \"scroll grouped icons\", which fails 9/16 frames without the ordinal.","files":null}]}